    "site_desc": "Regenerated jack pine (Pinus banksiana) following fire in 1977; canopy height 6 m and LAI = 2.8.  Some black spruce understory developing.  Trees tend to be clumpy, with some clear spaces that can be easily walked thorugh, and other areas are thick.  Fire killed coarse woody debris on the ground, that is soft and decomposing.  Very few perched trunks. Understory are short shrubs such as Vaccinium and Arctostaphylus uva-ursi.",
